**How to implement.** The shared test-support project is born, and S9.4's repository-root kit locator is its first source (001 §Q AT-2 'The ground truth and designs … move into a shared test-support project, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/`, one `.fsproj` in its own folder. Both `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` reference it, so one compiled copy serves both test suites'; 001 §S10 'create `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/` (own folder, own `.fsproj`, a plain library)'; .spec-md §3.21 'The helper lives in `BerremanTests` until S10 moves it to `BerremanTestSupport`'; the S10.2 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples (test → product / test support) … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one `CommittedKit` exists. (1) New `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj`, the only project file in its folder (AGENTS.md 'One `.fsproj` per folder'). It is a plain library, not a test project: no `OutputType`, `IsTestProject` or `UseMicrosoftTestingPlatformRunner` property and no test package. Its two property groups are those of `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj` (`OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj:3-14`) without the `AssemblyName` line: `TargetFramework` `net10.0`, `Platforms` `x64` and `IsPackable` `false`; and, for `Release|x64`, `OtherFlags` `--warnaserror+:25 --platform:x64`, `PlatformTarget` `x64` and `NoWarn` `NU5100;NU5110;NU5111;NU1903`. It keeps the SDK's default assembly name, `BerremanTestSupport`. One `ItemGroup` holds `<Compile Include="CommittedKits.fs" />`, and one holds the project reference to `..\OpticalConstructor\OpticalConstructor.Domain\OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` (`KitFolder` is Domain's, step 122). It has no package reference and no comment (AGENTS.md 'No new comments in `.fsproj`'), and like every file this section writes it has LF line endings (AGENTS.md 'Line endings: LF'). (2) `Berreman/Berreman.slnx` gains the entry `<Project Path="BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj">` holding `<Platform Project="x64" />`, in the shape of its neighbours, directly after the `BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj` entry (`Berreman.slnx:17-19`). (3) `git mv Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/CommittedKits.fs` (the file step 330 creates), and its namespace becomes `BerremanTestSupport`. Its opens, its one case `OpticsMuellerKit` and the body of `tryFindFolder` are unchanged. The locator therefore still walks up from `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory`, the folder of the running test assembly, and writes nothing. The type's doc says, in one to three lines, that these are the committed reference kits under the repository's `data/` folder, found from the folder holding `Berreman/Berreman.slnx` (spec 0050 §3.21, S9.4), and that both test suites share them through `BerremanTestSupport` (S10.2). The sentence saying that S10.2 moves it is deleted. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj` deletes `<Compile Include="CommittedKits.fs" />`. It gains the project reference to `..\BerremanTestSupport\BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` after its last `ProjectReference`, with no comment. (5) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` gains `open BerremanTestSupport` after its last `open` line, and nothing else in it changes. (6) Elevation. Nothing under `Elevation/` and nothing in `.elevation-analyzers.json` changes. The gate driver scopes every solution `.fsproj` whose name does not end in `Tests.fsproj` (`Elevation/Run-ElevationGate.ps1:151`), so it analyzes `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` too. The analyzers apply no rule to that assembly and report zero findings: its name matches neither `inScopePatterns` (`Softellect.Berreman.*`) nor `ownAssemblyPatterns` (`Softellect.*`) (`.elevation-analyzers.json:13-21`), and the same holds for the test projects. No `[<ElevationBoundary>]` or `[<NumericCarrier>]` mark is added to it. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the locator's body is unchanged. No test is added or removed. `MuellerReconstructionTests` is the one class that reaches the locator, through `loadDataSet` and through `the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte`.

**Acceptance.** After the project is created, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` MUST be a plain net10.0 x64 library with the assembly name `BerremanTestSupport`, listed in `Berreman.slnx`. It MUST compile `CommittedKits.fs` (namespace `BerremanTestSupport`) and be referenced by `BerremanTests`, and `Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST hold no `CommittedKits.fs`. unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s34 invariants MUST pass.
